inty wide.", "watch": "Fresh independent polling in October, or a shift in the national midterm environment, could move this back toward a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 74 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Jen Kiggans (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Virginia's 2nd District is a rematch-adjacent battleground where even partisan balance meets a midterm environment that has favored Democrats. Incumbent Jen Kiggans has out-raised Elaine Luria and holds a slight cash edge, but outside groups like Giffords PAC have invested heavily on Luria's side, and her campaign has centered on affordability and health care. Two minor independent candidates are on the ballot after a Luria challenge to their signatures failed to remove them.\n\nExpert ratings split between Tossup and Likely or Lean Democratic flip, and prediction markets price Luria's chances near 80 percent. The only available poll, a July survey with Democratic sponsorship, showed the race tied, so hard polling evidence remains scarce and the race could tighten as Kiggans's incumbency advantage and fundraising assert themselves.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7963, "margin": 4.98}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8168, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.777, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7659, "margin": 4.5}]}